---
// Every clause here is checkable against a product page. Keep it that way.
---

<section class="method wrap" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <h2 id="method-title" class="section-title method__title">How the studio works</h2>

  <div class="method__body">
    <p class="method__lead">
      There are no subscriptions here, and nothing is rented back to you. You pay
      once, if at all, and the software is yours.
    </p>
    <p>
      The heavy lifting happens on your own hardware. Beltr separates vocals on your
      computer; OneScribe reads your documents on your phone and never uploads them.
      Apple software is written in Swift for the device it runs on, not ported to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      And every project starts as a written specification. The thinking is done
      before the building begins, and the decisions are still on record when a
      product is five versions in.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .method {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
  }

  .method__title { padding-top: 0.5rem; }

  .method__body p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 34em;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.5vw, 1.3125rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }
  .method__body p + p { margin-top: 1.1em; }

  .method__body .method__lead {
    max-width: 22em;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.7vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 330;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .method { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
